---
/**
 * Contact (§4.4, §8).
 *
 * THE FORM POSTS TO FORMSPARK. This is a recorded deviation from §8, which
 * specifies a Cloudflare Pages Function with invisible Turnstile — see AUDIT.md
 * D7 for the reason and what was given up.
 *
 * §8's GUARANTEE IS UNCHANGED AND IS STILL THE POINT: a form that posts into an
 * unverified endpoint swallows a real enquiry SILENTLY, which is the most
 * expensive failure a marketing site has. What prevents that here is not a
 * disabled control — it is the INTERCEPTED SUBMIT plus the live status region.
 * `src/scripts/contact.ts` fetches with `accept: application/json`, Formspark
 * answers JSON rather than redirecting, and whatever comes back is rendered on
 * this page in words. Nothing is swallowed and nothing navigates away.
 *
 * That region is the whole guarantee, and `scripts/verify/contracts.mjs` fails
 * the build without it.
 *
 * THE ENDPOINT IS PUBLIC AND STATIC, so there is no "configured" state any more
 * and no env var gating this page. The form id is not a secret: it ships in the
 * `action` attribute of every contact page Formspark has ever documented. The
 * secret-bearing half of the old design — a Turnstile secret and a Resend key in
 * the Pages Function's env — no longer exists.
 *
 * NO TURNSTILE. It was removed with the Pages Function that verified it: the
 * token was only ever checked server-side by `functions/api/contact.ts`, and
 * Formspark does not check it. A challenge nobody verifies is a step the visitor
 * pays for and no bot is stopped by. Spam is now Formspark's built-in filtering
 * plus the honeypot below, which Formspark DOES enforce.
 *
 * NO CTA BAND: this page is the call to action. Copy is verbatim from Figma
 * 788:9565; the five controls are exactly the ones the design draws, mapped onto
 * FormField in the Phase 1 audit.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../components/shells/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import FormField from '../components/atoms/FormField.astro';
import Button from '../components/atoms/Button.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/atoms/TextLink.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

/**
 * The Formspark endpoint.
 *
 * NOT A SECRET and not an env var, which is worth saying once because the old
 * design's endpoint half was both. A Formspark form id is public by
 * construction — it is the `action` of a plain HTML form, visible in view-source
 * on every page that carries one. It is written here rather than in the
 * environment so the form works on a fresh clone with no setup, which is the
 * same reason `SITE.origin` is a constant.
 *
 * Changing the destination is changing this line.
 */
const FORM_ENDPOINT = 'https://submit-form.com/bqtIN0U6N';

/**
 * The honeypot field's name.
 *
 * IN THE FRONTMATTER, AND THAT IS NOT TIDINESS. This explanation sat beside the
 * input as an `<!-- -->` comment, and Astro emits those: **a paragraph naming
 * the honeypot field and explaining how the trap works was shipping in the HTML
 * of the live contact page**, readable by precisely the scrapers it exists to
 * catch. Frontmatter is compiled away and cannot leak; `{/* … *\/}` in the
 * template is stripped too. `<!-- … -->` is not.
 *
 * THE NAME IS THE MECHANISM. A honeypot works by looking like a field worth
 * filling. `_honeypot` and `_gotcha` are Formspark's always-on names and
 * therefore PUBLISHED ones — a bot author who has read any form using them can
 * skip them by name everywhere, and the better the bot the more certainly it
 * does. `company_contact` reads as an ordinary contact field, so there is
 * nothing to skip on sight.
 *
 * Registered as a custom honeypot name in the Formspark dashboard, which is what
 * makes it enforced rather than merely collected.
 *
 * THE COUPLING IS INVISIBLE FROM HERE: this is a trap only while that dashboard
 * setting exists. Remove the custom name in Formspark and this markup goes on
 * looking exactly as correct as it does now while quietly filing spam as
 * ordinary form data. Nothing in this repo can see that setting or assert it —
 * WORKLOG open question 65. Changing the name means changing it in both places,
 * and in `HONEYPOT_FIELD` in scripts/verify/contracts.mjs.
 *
 * It was `_honeypot`, and before that `company_website`, for the Pages Function
 * that no longer exists (AUDIT D7).
 */
const HONEYPOT = 'company_contact';

/**
 * The select's ranges are NOT in the design — only the placeholder is drawn.
 * Open question 14. These are a stand-in shaped like the placeholder promises
 * ("up to 10,000+") and flagged rather than presented as final.
 */
const SHIPMENT_RANGES = [
  'Under 500 / week',
  '500 – 2,000 / week',
  '2,000 – 5,000 / week',
  '5,000 – 10,000 / week',
  '10,000+ / week',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Contact — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="We come back with a recommended build and pricing. There is no automated sequence behind this form — it goes straight to the team."
>
  <Section spaceTop="nav" spaceBottom="lg">
    <div class="gap-2xl md:gap-xl md:grid md:grid-cols-12 flex flex-col">
      {/* Left: the promise. */}
      <div class="gap-xl md:col-span-5 flex flex-col">
        <div class="gap-md flex flex-col">
          <h1 class="text-h2 text-primary">Contact us now</h1>
          <p class="text-body text-secondary measure">
            No automated sequence — the form goes straight to the team, and you get a build and
            pricing back, typically within one business day.
          </p>
        </div>

        <hr class="border-line w-full border-t" />

        <p class="gap-xl text-body flex">
          <span class="text-secondary">Email:</span>
          <TextLink href="mailto:info@centipack.com">info@centipack.com</TextLink>
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Right: the form, on its own ground. */}
      <div class="bg-subtle rounded-md p-lg md:p-2xl md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7">

        <form
          method="POST"
          action={FORM_ENDPOINT}
          data-contact-form
          class="gap-lg flex flex-col"
        >
          {/* See HONEYPOT in the frontmatter. This comment form is stripped at
              build; an HTML comment would not be. */}
          <div class="sr-only" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for={HONEYPOT}>Leave this field empty</label>
            <input id={HONEYPOT} type="text" name={HONEYPOT} tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>

          <FormField
            label="Full Name"
            name="name"
            required
            autocomplete="name"
            placeholder="Your name"
          />
          <FormField
            label="Work email"
            name="email"
            type="email"
            required
            autocomplete="email"
            inputmode="email"
            placeholder="you@pharmacy.com"
          />
          <FormField
            label="Company"
            name="company"
            autocomplete="organization"
            placeholder="Pharmacy or brand name"
          />
          <FormField
            label="Projected shipments per week"
            name="volume"
            type="select"
            placeholder="Select a range — up to 10,000+"
            options={SHIPMENT_RANGES}
          />
          <FormField
            label="What are you shipping, and where?"
            name="message"
            type="textarea"
            rows={5}
            placeholder="e.g. GLP-1 injectables, nationwide next-day air, 3,000 packages/week"
          />

          <Button type="submit" variant="primary" icon="square" iconPosition="start" class="w-full">
            Send request
          </Button>

          {/*
            THE ANSWER HAS TO LAND SOMEWHERE ON THIS PAGE.

            The endpoint replies with JSON, and a native form POST to a JSON
            response NAVIGATES — the visitor would have left the site and be
            looking at `{"ok":true}` in a blank tab. That was the shipped
            behaviour, and `contact.ts` described it as "a redirect-friendly
            status", which the endpoint has never returned.

            `role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"` so the reply is announced
            rather than only drawn. It is empty and `hidden` at rest, so it
            occupies nothing until there is something to say.
          */}
          <p
            data-contact-status
            role="status"
            aria-live="polite"
            class="text-sm text-secondary"
            hidden
          />
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/contact';
</script>

{/* The Turnstile script tag was here. It went with the Pages Function that
    verified its token — nothing checks it now, so loading it would be a
    third-party request on the launch page's critical path buying nothing. */}
